%!PS-Adobe-3.0
%%Title: drykit.ps — dry media core: a stick drawn across a toothed surface
%%Creator: pscat — issue #234 (design: docs/dev/design/DRYMEDIA.md)
%%EndComments
%
% Every procedure here is defined `} bind def` (issue #307). Ghostscript
% looks up each executable name in a procedure body at run time, and
% those lookups are slow once userdict holds the libraries' several
% hundred names; `bind` resolves the operators once, when the library
% loads. The cost: an operator redefined *after* this file loads (a
% caller's own `/show`, `/rand`, `/fill`) no longer reaches these
% procedures, and one redefined *before* it loads is left alone, since
% `bind` only replaces names that are operators at that moment. Names
% that are not operators (every library procedure, and tunables such as
% drykit's `dkbudget`) stay late-bound, so overriding those works as
% before. tests/libbind.rs fails for any procedure added without `bind`.
% @requires: (lib/artkit.ps) run (lib/paintkit.ps) run

% The shared engine under chalk, crayon and charcoal (epic #232). A dry
% stick deposits pigment only where its contact patch meets raised tooth,
% so drykit builds every mark through a *catch*: a clip made of the
% knuckles of the surface that the stick reaches at a given touch.
%
% The surface is paintkit's (#182, docs/dev/design/CANVAS_SURFACE.md): one `pkcanvas`
% height field in canvas space, so a piece that mixes paintkit and drykit
% marks has one canvas, and two crossing strokes break up on the same
% tooth whichever library drew them. drykit never edits lib/paintkit.ps.
% It reads these @internal names, and the `drykit-paintkit-contract`
% self-test below pins each one (DRYMEDIA.md Q1; #270 moves them to
% lib/toothkit.ps):
%
%   pjheight  i j -> 0..1      the knuckle height of cell (i, j)
%   pjhash    i j s -> 0..1    the per-cell hash, read through /pjp
%   pjCTM pjP pjW pjM pjR      canvas space, permutation, /Weave, /Mottle,
%                              /Relief, as pkcanvas leaves them in userdict
%   pjmemo                     the height memo pjheight fills
%
% Public: `dksurface` (the named surfaces), `dkstroke` (a stroke) and
% `dkbatch` (strokes drawn level-major together). Internal: `dkcatch`, the
% catch every stroke is drawn through, and `dkrand`, the private generator.
%
% `dkcatch` differs from paintkit's `pjcatch` in two ways (DRYMEDIA.md 2.1):
%
% * Oriented knuckles. Each knuckle is an ellipse whose long axis follows
%   the direction of travel, stretched by `streak`: skipped valleys read as
%   streaks along the stroke (reference board M2), not round pits. The
%   selection rule and the scale law are pjcatch's, unchanged, so a knuckle
%   is selected at exactly the same touch in both, and catches over the
%   same stops nest: catch(t1) is inside catch(t2) for t1 < t2. A knuckle
%   takes the orientation of the nearest segment among those whose reach
%   covers its cell. When every stop has the same half-width that is the
%   nearest segment outright, whatever the touch or a uniform widening. When
%   half-widths vary along a run, a wider catch can bring a nearer, thinner
%   segment into reach and turn a knuckle, so nesting is not guaranteed
%   there (tests/drykit.rs measures it under a /Pressure run: none seen).
% * Swept-band cells. It visits only the cells whose centre lies within
%   reach of the centerline -- per segment, the exact column-by-column
%   interval of its capsule -- not every cell of the mark's bounding box.
%   A cell is visited once per segment that reaches it and built once.
%
% The reach from a segment is the stroke's own half-width plus the
% farthest a knuckle extends from its cell centre (0.88 grow streak W for
% the stretched long semi-axis, plus 0.22W for the centre's nudge) plus
% `dkslack` device pixels (0 unless a test asks for pixel identity; see
% its definition).
%
% Ghostscript closes sub-2-pixel gaps in fills and clips (its fill adjust),
% which turns a fine catch into a solid stroke. dkcatch turns it off with
% the guarded `/.setfilladjust2 where { pop 0 0 .setfilladjust2 } if` just
% before its `clip` (DRYMEDIA.md 2.4, Q8); it is a gs internal, absent in
% pscat, and it lives in the caller's gsave like the clip does.
%
% Determinism. drykit takes no draws from the caller's `rand` stream. The
% surface takes no draws at all; the tool-side generator (`dkrand`, for
% the contact chains and fallout seeds) is the same Schrage-form minimal
% standard LCG as paintkit's `pjrand`, under its own state in userdict;
% and fallout goes through artkit's `scatter` with a /Seed, which seeds
% `rand` and restores the caller's stream afterwards.
%
% Scratch prefix dk-. Every name is distinct from the pk*/pj*/pu* families,
% so nothing paintkit runs (pjheight's own scratch, a preset drawn in the
% same piece, pkribbon's habit of clobbering pk* names) can reach it.
% dkstroke builds its own ink geometry and does not call pkribbon
% (DRYMEDIA.md 3.3 allowed for it; a union of discs and quads keeps the ink
% exactly within the reach the catch is cut for).

% Unique cells one catch may build. Past it dkcatch rejects; a caller with a
% larger mark splits it into several catches.
% @internal
/dkbudget 150000 def

% Extra reach, in device pixels. 0 for rendering. The clip mask is
% anti-aliased, so a knuckle that ends within a pixel of the ink, without
% touching it, still shades that edge pixel; a test that wants pixel
% identity against a whole-page catch sets 1.5 (more than a pixel's
% diagonal). At 144 dpi 1.5 pixels is 0.75pt of reach on each side, which
% cost the full board 60% more cells (docs/dev/design/DRYMEDIA.md 6.1) for a
% sub-pixel difference at the ink's edge.
% @internal
/dkslack 0 def

% any -> bool   (an integer or a real)
% @internal
/dkisnum {
    type dup /integertype eq exch /realtype eq or
} bind def

% dict key default -> value   (the default when the key is absent)
% @internal
/dkget {
    /dkgd exch def
    2 copy known { get } { pop pop /dkgd load } ifelse
} bind def

% a b -> max(a, b)
% @internal
/dkmax {
    2 copy lt { exch } if pop
} bind def

% a b -> min(a, b)
% @internal
/dkmin {
    2 copy gt { exch } if pop
} bind def

% seed -   (seeds drykit's own generator)
% Same shape as paintkit's pjsrand: reduced mod 2147483646 before `abs`, and
% offset to 1..2147483646, because 0 is the Lehmer generator's fixed point.
% The state lives in userdict, so a `begin ... end` around the caller can't
% take it away mid-stroke.
% @internal
/dksrand {
    cvi 2147483646 mod abs 1 add
    userdict /dkstate 3 -1 roll put
} bind def

% -> 0.0..1.0   (exclusive at both ends)
% Schrage's decomposition of (16807, 2^31 - 1), so every intermediate fits
% in Ghostscript's 32-bit integers and both interpreters draw the same
% sequence. The caller's `rand` stream is never touched.
% @internal
/dkrand {
    userdict /dkstate get
    dup 127773 idiv 2836 mul exch 127773 mod 16807 mul exch sub
    dup 0 lt { 2147483647 add } if
    dup userdict /dkstate 3 -1 roll put
    2147483647 div
} bind def

% The generator's state, as `1 dksrand` leaves it, so dkrand works before
% anything seeds it.
% @internal
/dkstate 2 def

% The named surfaces (DRYMEDIA.md 2.3): plain pkcanvas keys plus the
% surface's own colour. Starting values from the reference board, with
% /Relief raised where the shared-tooth test needed it: Q4 (mean phi >= 0.4
% between crossing strokes) failed on newsprint at 0.4 and passes at 0.55,
% the boards' value (tests/drykit.rs test 1 checks every surface).
% /drawing's /Mottle is 1.5, not 6 (#313): at 6 the slow mottle opened white
% islands several points across in fine hatching, which no reference shows
% (H2, H4 break up as specks). A smaller mottle scale keeps /Relief 0.65, so
% crossing strokes still share their tooth (Q4), while the patches shrink
% to a few knuckles. Lowering /Relief to 0.35 also cured the islands but
% put Q4 at 0.34. The mottle lattice repeats every 256 x /Mottle (384 pt).
% @internal
/dksurfaces <<
    /slate        << /Weave 0.4  /Relief 0.55 /Mottle 4 /Ground [0.13 0.14 0.16] >>
    /greenboard   << /Weave 0.4  /Relief 0.55 /Mottle 4 /Ground [0.17 0.23 0.20] >>
    /newsprint    << /Weave 0.35 /Relief 0.55 /Mottle 3 /Ground [0.86 0.84 0.78] >>
    /drawing      << /Weave 0.6  /Relief 0.65 /Mottle 1.5 /Ground [0.95 0.94 0.90] >>
    /construction << /Weave 0.9  /Relief 0.75 /Mottle 8 /Ground [0.20 0.34 0.62] >>
>> def

% a b c d -> the largest singular value of the 2x2 map [a b; c d]
% (how far it can stretch a unit length, whatever the direction)
% @internal
/dksvmax {
    /dkvd exch def /dkvc exch def /dkvb exch def /dkva exch def
    /dkvt dkva dup mul dkvb dup mul add dkvc dup mul add dkvd dup mul add def
    /dkvq dkva dkvd mul dkvb dkvc mul sub def
    dkvt dup mul dkvq dup mul 4 mul sub dup 0 lt { pop 0 } if sqrt
    dkvt add 2 div sqrt
} bind def

% px py -   (widen dklo..dkhi by the reach disc about p, on column dkx)
% @internal
/dkdisc {
    /dkey0 exch def /dkex0 exch def
    /dkq dkR2 dkx dkex0 sub dup mul sub def
    dkq 0 ge {
        /dkq dkq sqrt def
        dkey0 dkq sub dup dklo lt { /dklo exch def } { pop } ifelse
        dkey0 dkq add dup dkhi gt { /dkhi exch def } { pop } ifelse
    } if
} bind def

% ox oy -   (widen dklo..dkhi by the segment offset by (ox, oy), on dkx)
% The capsule is convex, so its column interval runs between the extremes
% of the pieces that bound it: the two end discs and the two offset sides.
% @internal
/dkside {
    /dkoy exch def /dkox exch def
    /dkpax dkax dkox add def
    /dkpbx dkbx dkox add def
    dkpbx dkpax sub abs 1e-12 gt {
        dkx dkpax sub dkpbx dkpax sub div
        dup 0 ge exch dup 1 le 3 -1 roll and {
            dkby dkay sub mul dkay add dkoy add
            dup dklo lt { dup /dklo exch def } if
            dup dkhi gt { dup /dkhi exch def } if
            pop
        } { pop } ifelse
    } if
} bind def

% j -   (offer cell (dkci, j) to the catch from segment dkseg)
% Records the cell on first sight, and keeps the nearest segment's index for
% its orientation (ties keep the lower index, since segments come in order).
% @internal
/dkcell {
    /dkcj exch def
    /dkcyy dkcj 0.5 add dkW mul def
    dkl2 0 gt {
        dkx dkax sub dkdx mul dkcyy dkay sub dkdy mul add dkl2 div
        dup 0 lt { pop 0 } if dup 1 gt { pop 1 } if
        /dkt0 exch def
        dkx dkax sub dkdx dkt0 mul sub dup mul
        dkcyy dkay sub dkdy dkt0 mul sub dup mul add
    } {
        dkx dkax sub dup mul dkcyy dkay sub dup mul add
    } ifelse
    /dkd2 exch def
    /dkkey dkci dki0 sub 32768 mul dkcj dkj0 sub add def
    dkseen dkkey known {
        dkseen dkkey get /dkslot exch def
        dkdistbuf dkslot get dkd2 gt {
            dkdistbuf dkslot dkd2 put
            dksegbuf dkslot dkseg put
        } if
    } {
        dkn dkcap ge { dkcatch-area-exceeds-safety-limit } if
        dkseen dkkey dkn put
        dkkeybuf dkn dkkey put
        dkdistbuf dkn dkd2 put
        dksegbuf dkn dkseg put
        /dkn dkn 1 add def
    } ifelse
} bind def

% a b -   (one centerline segment between canvas stops [x y reach])
% @internal
/dkseg1 {
    /dksb exch def /dksa exch def
    /dkax dksa 0 get def /dkay dksa 1 get def
    /dkbx dksb 0 get def /dkby dksb 1 get def
    /dkR dksa 2 get dksb 2 get dkmax def
    /dkR2 dkR dup mul def
    /dkdx dkbx dkax sub def /dkdy dkby dkay sub def
    /dkl2 dkdx dup mul dkdy dup mul add def
    dkl2 1e-18 gt {
        /dkl dkl2 sqrt def
        /dkux dkdx dkl div def /dkuy dkdy dkl div def
    } {
        % a point: the run's previous direction (or +x) orients it
        /dkl2 0 def
    } ifelse
    dkuxs dkseg dkux put
    dkuys dkseg dkuy put
    dkax dkbx dkmin dkR sub dkW div 0.5 sub ceiling cvi
    1
    dkax dkbx dkmax dkR add dkW div 0.5 sub floor cvi
    {
        /dkci exch def
        /dkx dkci 0.5 add dkW mul def
        /dklo 1e30 def /dkhi -1e30 def
        dkax dkay dkdisc
        dkbx dkby dkdisc
        dkl2 0 gt {
            dkuy neg dkR mul dkux dkR mul dkside
            dkuy dkR mul dkux neg dkR mul dkside
        } if
        dklo dkhi le {
            dklo dkW div 0.5 sub ceiling cvi
            1
            dkhi dkW div 0.5 sub floor cvi
            { dkcell } for
        } if
    } for
    /dkseg dkseg 1 add def
} bind def

% x y -   (widen the canvas box dkx0..dky1 by a canvas point)
% @internal
/dkgrowbox {
    dup dky0 lt { dup /dky0 exch def } if
    dup dky1 gt { dup /dky1 exch def } if
    pop
    dup dkx0 lt { dup /dkx0 exch def } if
    dup dkx1 gt { dup /dkx1 exch def } if
    pop
} bind def

% -   (the band pass: every guard and every cell, with no graphics state
% changed, so a rejected catch leaves the caller's clip and CTM alone)
% @internal
/dkband {
    /dkW userdict /pjW get def
    /pjp userdict /pjP get def
    /dkcm userdict /pjCTM get def
    /dkgrow dkct 0.8 sub 0.2 div dup 0 lt { pop 0 } if 0.25 mul 1 add def
    % user-space lengths to canvas lengths, and one device pixel in canvas
    1 0 dtransform dkcm idtransform 0 1 dtransform dkcm idtransform dksvmax
    /dkhs exch def
    1 0 dkcm idtransform 0 1 dkcm idtransform dksvmax
    /dkpx exch def
    /dkpad dkpx dkslack mul def
    /dkK dkgrow dkcs mul 0.88 mul 0.22 add dkW mul dkpad add def
    /dkwhole userdict /pjWholePage known def

    % Pre-pass: every stop to canvas space as [x y reach], with the box.
    /dkx0 1e30 def /dky0 1e30 def /dkx1 -1e30 def /dky1 -1e30 def
    /dknseg 0 def
    /dkrmax 0 def
    /dkcv [
        dkcr {
            /dkrun exch def
            /dkrun load type /arraytype ne { dkcatch-run-must-be-an-array } if
            /dkrun load xcheck { dkcatch-run-must-be-an-array } if
            /dknseg dknseg dkrun length 1 sub 1 dkmax add def
            [
                dkrun {
                    /dkstop exch def
                    /dkstop load type /arraytype ne { dkcatch-stop-must-be-x-y-halfwidth } if
                    /dkstop load xcheck { dkcatch-stop-must-be-x-y-halfwidth } if
                    dkstop length 3 lt { dkcatch-stop-must-be-x-y-halfwidth } if
                    dkstop 0 get dkisnum dkstop 1 get dkisnum and dkstop 2 get dkisnum and
                        not { dkcatch-stop-must-be-x-y-halfwidth } if
                    dkstop 2 get 0 lt { dkcatch-halfwidth-must-not-be-negative } if
                    dkstop 0 get dkstop 1 get transform dkcm itransform
                    /dksy exch def /dksx exch def
                    /dksr dkstop 2 get dkhs mul dkK add def
                    dksr dkrmax gt { /dkrmax dksr def } if
                    dksx dksy dkgrowbox
                    [ dksx dksy dksr ]
                } forall
            ]
            dup length 0 eq { pop /dknseg dknseg 1 sub def } if
        } forall
    ] def
    % A segment reaches as far as its wider end, so the box grows by the
    % widest reach of any stop, not each stop's own: a thin end next to a
    % wide one would otherwise leave cells outside the key range.
    dkx0 dkx1 le {
        /dkx0 dkx0 dkrmax sub def /dky0 dky0 dkrmax sub def
        /dkx1 dkx1 dkrmax add def /dky1 dky1 dkrmax add def
    } if
    % Test-only (CANVAS_SURFACE.md 6, test 7): with userdict /pjWholePage
    % set, every cell under the current clip joins too, so a test can
    % check that the band clipped no paint. No library code sets it.
    % The clip's box is taken in canvas space directly, not as a user-space
    % box's corners, which in a rotated or sheared space bounds far more.
    dkwhole {
        gsave dkcm setmatrix clippath pathbbox grestore
        /dkwy1 exch def /dkwx1 exch def /dkwy0 exch def /dkwx0 exch def
        dkwx0 dkwy0 dkgrowbox
        dkwx1 dkwy1 dkgrowbox
    } if

    /dkn 0 def
    dkx0 dkx1 le {
        [ dkx0 dky0 dkx1 dky1 ] {
            dkW div abs 1e9 gt { dkcatch-area-exceeds-safety-limit } if
        } forall
        /dki0 dkx0 dkW div floor cvi 1 sub def
        /dkj0 dky0 dkW div floor cvi 1 sub def
        /dki1 dkx1 dkW div floor cvi 1 add def
        /dkj1 dky1 dkW div floor cvi 1 add def
        dki1 dki0 sub 32768 ge dkj1 dkj0 sub 32768 ge or
            { dkcatch-area-exceeds-safety-limit } if
        dkwhole {
            /dkcap dki1 dki0 sub 1 add dkj1 dkj0 sub 1 add mul def
            dkcap 4000000 gt { dkcatch-area-exceeds-safety-limit } if
        } {
            /dkcap dkbudget def
        } ifelse
        % Scratch buffers are kept between calls: allocating them per catch
        % costs more than a small catch does.
        userdict /dkkeybuf known { userdict /dkkeybuf get length dkcap lt } { true } ifelse {
            userdict /dkkeybuf dkcap array put
            userdict /dkdistbuf dkcap array put
            userdict /dksegbuf dkcap array put
        } if
        /dkkeybuf userdict /dkkeybuf get def
        /dkdistbuf userdict /dkdistbuf get def
        /dksegbuf userdict /dksegbuf get def
        /dkuxs dknseg 1 dkmax array def
        /dkuys dknseg 1 dkmax array def
        /dkseen 1024 dict def
        /dkseg 0 def
        dkcv {
            /dkrv exch def
            /dkux 1 def /dkuy 0 def
            dkrv length 1 eq { dkrv 0 get dkrv 0 get dkseg1 } if
            dkrv length 1 gt {
                0 1 dkrv length 2 sub {
                    /dkri exch def
                    dkrv dkri get dkrv dkri 1 add get dkseg1
                } for
            } if
        } forall
        dkwhole {
            dki0 1 dki1 {
                /dkci exch def
                dkj0 1 dkj1 {
                    /dkkey exch dkj0 sub dkci dki0 sub 32768 mul add def
                    dkseen dkkey known not {
                        dkseen dkkey dkn put
                        dkkeybuf dkn dkkey put
                        dksegbuf dkn -1 put
                        /dkn dkn 1 add def
                    } if
                } for
            } for
        } if
    } if
} bind def

% -   (appends the knuckle at dkcx dkcy: semi-axes dkea along (dkex, dkey),
% dkeb across it, as four curveto's in the current (canvas) space)
% @internal
/dkoval {
    /dk1x dkex dkea mul def /dk1y dkey dkea mul def
    /dk2x dkey neg dkeb mul def /dk2y dkex dkeb mul def
    /dkm1x dk1x 0.5523 mul def /dkm1y dk1y 0.5523 mul def
    /dkm2x dk2x 0.5523 mul def /dkm2y dk2y 0.5523 mul def
    /dkX1 dkcx dk1x add def /dkY1 dkcy dk1y add def
    /dkX2 dkcx dk2x add def /dkY2 dkcy dk2y add def
    /dkX3 dkcx dk1x sub def /dkY3 dkcy dk1y sub def
    /dkX4 dkcx dk2x sub def /dkY4 dkcy dk2y sub def
    dkX1 dkY1 moveto
    dkX1 dkm2x add dkY1 dkm2y add dkX2 dkm1x add dkY2 dkm1y add dkX2 dkY2 curveto
    dkX2 dkm1x sub dkY2 dkm1y sub dkX3 dkm2x add dkY3 dkm2y add dkX3 dkY3 curveto
    dkX3 dkm2x sub dkY3 dkm2y sub dkX4 dkm1x sub dkY4 dkm1y sub dkX4 dkY4 curveto
    dkX4 dkm1x add dkY4 dkm1y add dkX1 dkm2x sub dkY1 dkm2y sub dkX1 dkY1 curveto
    closepath
} bind def

% -   (builds the knuckles the band pass recorded and clips to them)
% Cells are built in the order they were first seen, never in dict order,
% so the clip path -- and an SVG or PDF of it -- is the same on every run.
% Keep the list even though pscat's dict forall is insertion-ordered now
% (#277): drykit also runs in Ghostscript, whose forall over integer keys is
% hash order. Raster output matches either way; Ghostscript's pdfwrite
% output does not, and the order would stop being the algorithm's own
% (notes/287-dkcatch-first-seen-list-kept.md).
% @internal
/dkemit {
    /dksaved matrix currentmatrix def
    dkcm setmatrix
    newpath
    /dkk 0 def
    0 1 dkn 1 sub {
        /dkq exch def
        /dkkey dkkeybuf dkq get def
        /dkci dkkey 32768 idiv dki0 add def
        /dkcj dkkey 32768 mod dkj0 add def
        /dkd dkci dkcj pjheight dkct add 1 sub def
        dkd 0 gt {
            /dks dkd 0.3 div dup 1 gt { pop 1 } if 0.5 mul 0.6 add
                dkgrow mul dkW mul def
            /dkcx dkci 0.5 add dkci dkcj 2 pjhash 0.5 sub 0.3 mul add dkW mul def
            /dkcy dkcj 0.5 add dkci dkcj 3 pjhash 0.5 sub 0.3 mul add dkW mul def
            /dkea dks 0.8 mul dkcs mul def
            /dkg dksegbuf dkq get def
            dkg 0 ge {
                /dkeb dks 0.42 mul def
                /dkex dkuxs dkg get def /dkey dkuys dkg get def
            } {
                % whole-page test cells: a disc as long as the longest
                % knuckle, so it reaches as far as any orientation could
                /dkeb dkea def /dkex 1 def /dkey 0 def
            } ifelse
            dkoval
            /dkk dkk 1 add def
        } if
    } for
    dkk 0 eq { 0 0 moveto 0 0 lineto } if
    /.setfilladjust2 where { pop 0 0 .setfilladjust2 } if
    clip newpath
    dksaved setmatrix
} bind def

%%SelfTest: drykit-paintkit-contract
%   % DRYMEDIA.md Q1: drykit reads these paintkit @internal names. If one is
%   % renamed or changes shape, this fails here rather than in a render.
%   << /Seed 5 /Weave 0.5 /Mottle 4 /Relief 0.6 >> pkcanvas
%   userdict /pjCTM get type /arraytype eq userdict /pjCTM get length 6 eq and
%   (pjCTM is a 6-element matrix) mustbe
%   userdict /pjP get type /arraytype eq userdict /pjP get length 256 eq and
%   (pjP is a 256-entry permutation) mustbe
%   userdict /pjW get 0.5 eq userdict /pjM get 4 eq and userdict /pjR get 0.6 eq and
%   (pjW pjM pjR hold /Weave /Mottle /Relief) mustbe
%   userdict /pjmemo get type /dicttype eq
%   (pjmemo is a dict) mustbe
%
%   count /dktn exch def
%   3 -7 pjheight
%   count dktn 1 add eq
%   (pjheight takes i j and leaves one value) mustbe
%   dup dkisnum exch dup 0 ge exch 1 le and and
%   (that value is a number in 0..1) mustbe
%   3 -7 pjheight 3 -7 pjheight eq
%   (pjheight is a pure function of the cell) mustbe
%   userdict /pjmemo get length 0 gt
%   (pjheight fills pjmemo) mustbe
%
%   /pjp userdict /pjP get def
%   count /dktn exch def
%   3 -7 2 pjhash
%   count dktn 1 add eq
%   (pjhash takes i j s through /pjp and leaves one value) mustbe
%   dup 0 ge exch 1 le and
%   (that value is in 0..1) mustbe
%%EndSelfTest
%
%%SelfTest: dkrand-is-private-and-matches-pjrand
%   1 srand rand /dkta exch def
%   1 srand 77 dksrand dkrand pop dkrand pop rand dkta eq
%   (dksrand and dkrand leave the caller's stream untouched) mustbe
%
%   77 dksrand dkrand dkrand dkrand /dktc exch def /dktb exch def /dkta exch def
%   77 pjsrand pjrand dkta eq pjrand dktb eq and pjrand dktc eq and
%   (dkrand is pjrand's generator under its own state) mustbe
%
%   0 dksrand dkrand dup 0 gt exch 1 lt and
%   (a zero seed is moved off the generator's fixed point) mustbe
%%EndSelfTest
%
%%SelfTest: dkcatch-guards
%   % touch >= 1 does nothing, even with no canvas set.
%   { gsave [ [ [0 0 1] ] ] 1 1.4 dkcatch grestore } (touch 1 with no canvas) mustpass
%
%   { [ [ [0 0 1] ] ] 0.5 1.4 dkcatch } /dkcatch-needs-a-canvas
%   (a catch before any pkcanvas) mustguard
%
%   << >> pkcanvas
%   { [ [ [0 0 1] ] ] (x) 1.4 dkcatch } /dkcatch-touch-must-be-a-number
%   (a string touch) mustguard
%
%   { [ [ [0 0 1] ] ] { 0.5 } 1.4 dkcatch } /dkcatch-touch-must-be-a-number
%   (a procedure touch) mustguard
%
%   { [ [ [0 0 1] ] ] 0.5 0.9 dkcatch } /dkcatch-streak-must-be-1-to-4
%   (/Streak below 1) mustguard
%
%   { [ [ [0 0 1] ] ] 0.5 4.5 dkcatch } /dkcatch-streak-must-be-1-to-4
%   (/Streak above 4) mustguard
%
%   { [ [ [0 0 1] ] ] 0.5 /x dkcatch } /dkcatch-streak-must-be-a-number
%   (a name streak) mustguard
%
%   { { } 0.5 1.4 dkcatch } /dkcatch-runs-must-be-an-array
%   (a procedure for the runs) mustguard
%
%   { [ 5 ] 0.5 1.4 dkcatch } /dkcatch-run-must-be-an-array
%   (a run that is a number) mustguard
%
%   { [ [ [0 0] ] ] 0.5 1.4 dkcatch } /dkcatch-stop-must-be-x-y-halfwidth
%   (a stop with two slots) mustguard
%
%   { [ [ [0 (y) 1] ] ] 0.5 1.4 dkcatch } /dkcatch-stop-must-be-x-y-halfwidth
%   (a stop with a string slot) mustguard
%
%   { [ [ [0 0 -1] ] ] 0.5 1.4 dkcatch } /dkcatch-halfwidth-must-not-be-negative
%   (a negative half-width) mustguard
%
%   { [ [ [0 0 1] [1e12 0 1] ] ] 0.5 1.4 dkcatch } /dkcatch-area-exceeds-safety-limit
%   (a segment past cvi's range) mustguard
%
%   { [ [ [0 0 1] [100000 0 1] ] ] 0.5 1.4 dkcatch } /dkcatch-area-exceeds-safety-limit
%   (a segment longer than the key span) mustguard
%
%   % The budget is lowered for the block, so the band that crosses it is
%   % cheap to build; the shipped 150000 cells is about 4 s of pscat.
%   /dkbudget 500 def
%   { [ [ [0 0 20] [100 0 20] ] ] 0.5 1.4 dkcatch } /dkcatch-area-exceeds-safety-limit
%   (a band past the cell budget) mustguard
%   { gsave [ [ [0 0 1] [10 0 1] ] ] 0.5 1.4 dkcatch grestore } (a band inside it) mustpass
%
%   { gsave [ ] 0.5 1.4 dkcatch grestore } (no runs: an empty clip) mustpass
%   { gsave [ [ ] ] 0.5 1.4 dkcatch grestore } (an empty run) mustpass
%   { gsave [ [ [10 10 2] ] ] 0.5 1.4 dkcatch grestore } (a one-stop run) mustpass
%   { gsave [ [ [10 10 2] [10 10 2] ] ] 0.5 1.4 dkcatch grestore } (a zero-length run) mustpass
%   { gsave [ [ [10 10 0] [60 30 0] ] ] 0.5 4 dkcatch grestore } (zero width at streak 4) mustpass
%%EndSelfTest
%
%%SelfTest: dkcatch-takes-no-draws-and-keeps-the-ctm
%   << /Seed 3 >> pkcanvas
%   1 srand rand /dkta exch def
%   1 srand gsave [ [ [0 0 2] [50 20 3] [80 0 2] ] ] 0.6 1.4 dkcatch grestore
%   rand dkta eq
%   (dkcatch leaves the caller's stream untouched) mustbe
%
%   gsave 7.5 0 translate 2 0.5 scale 15 rotate
%   matrix currentmatrix /dktm exch def
%   [ [ [0 0 2] [40 10 2] ] ] 0.5 1.8 dkcatch
%   matrix currentmatrix /dktn exch def
%   grestore
%   true 0 1 5 { dup dktm exch get exch dktn exch get eq and } for
%   (the CTM after dkcatch is the CTM before it) mustbe
%
%   % A rejected catch changes nothing: the guard runs before the matrix
%   % or the clip is touched.
%   /dkbudget 500 def
%   gsave 3 3 scale
%   matrix currentmatrix /dktm exch def
%   { [ [ [0 0 20] [100 0 20] ] ] 0.5 1.4 dkcatch } /dkcatch-area-exceeds-safety-limit
%   (a band past the budget, scaled) mustguard
%   matrix currentmatrix /dktn exch def
%   grestore
%   true 0 1 5 { dup dktm exch get exch dktn exch get eq and } for
%   (a rejected catch leaves the CTM alone) mustbe
%%EndSelfTest

% runs touch streak dkcatch -   (intersects the clip with the catch)
% runs is an array of runs, each an array of stops [x y halfwidth ...] in
% the current user space (slots past the third are ignored, so a stroke's
% own stop records can be passed as they are). Consecutive stops of a run
% are one centerline segment; a one-stop run is a dot. halfwidth is how far
% the mark's ink reaches from its centerline at that stop, in user-space
% points, and a segment reaches as far as its wider end.
%
% Every knuckle with d = height + touch - 1 > 0 within reach joins the clip,
% at pjcatch's scale (0.6 + 0.5 min(1, d/0.3)) (1 + 0.25 max(0,
% (touch - 0.8)/0.2)), its long axis 0.8 scale streak along its nearest
% segment and its short axis 0.42 scale across it. At touch >= 1 it does
% nothing; with no knuckle passing the clip becomes empty. Replaces the
% current path and leaves the CTM as it found it. streak is 1..4.
% @internal
/dkcatch {
    /dkcs exch def /dkct exch def /dkcr exch def
    /dkcr load type /arraytype ne { dkcatch-runs-must-be-an-array } if
    /dkcr load xcheck { dkcatch-runs-must-be-an-array } if
    /dkct load dkisnum not { dkcatch-touch-must-be-a-number } if
    /dkcs load dkisnum not { dkcatch-streak-must-be-a-number } if
    dkcs 1 lt dkcs 4 gt or { dkcatch-streak-must-be-1-to-4 } if
    dkct 1 lt {
        userdict /pjCTM known not { dkcatch-needs-a-canvas } if
        dkband
        dkemit
    } if
} bind def

% ---------------------------------------------------------------- dkstroke
%
% A stroke is resolved into a *record* before anything is drawn
% (DRYMEDIA.md 3.3): the path is walked once, each stop's touch, width and
% lane contacts are resolved once (a caller's /Touch or /Pressure procedure
% runs exactly once per stop, HANDOFF's "/Pressure inside a loop"), and the
% result is a list of runs, each `[key [ [x y hw] ... ]]`, where key is the
% run's touch band (plus its lane's tilt offset). The record also keeps the
% CTM the stroke was given in, so a batch can render it later from inside
% another gsave. Rendering (`dkrender`) then draws every record of a call,
% or of a whole `dkbatch`, level-major: all the faint levels first, then the
% brighter ones, so a later stroke's dim level never covers an earlier
% stroke's bright core. Within a pass, runs that share a touch, streak and
% colour share one catch (chunked under `dkbudget`), so overlapping strokes
% visit each cell once.
%
% Tool-side randomness (the contact chain of each lane) comes from
% `dkrand`, seeded per subpath: from `/Seed` plus the subpath's index when
% /Seed is given, else from the subpath's first point in canvas space, to
% 0.01pt, so adding a stroke elsewhere never re-rolls this one and a
% subpath draws the same whether it came in one call or in a batch. Each
% lane takes its own sub-seed and exactly one draw per stop, whatever the
% chain does with it. Fallout goes through artkit's `scatter`, whose /Seed
% restores the caller's stream.
%
% Scratch prefixes: dkS for the walk and the record, dkZ for rendering, so
% neither collides with dkcatch's names, which run in the middle of both.

% mark x1 .. xn -> [x1 .. xn]   (`]` for a mark pushed in another
% procedure or branch; build.rs's scanner pairs brackets lexically)
% @internal
/dktomark {
    counttomark array astore exch pop
} bind def

% n -> real   (a lane's or a piece's sub-seed from a subpath seed)
% @internal
/dksubseed {
    7919 mul dkSseed 1073741823 mod abs add dksrand dkrand pop
} bind def

% canvas coordinate -> 0..46336   (to 0.01pt, folded for a 31-bit seed)
% @internal
/dkSquant {
    100 mul round dup abs 2e9 gt { pop 0 } if cvi 46337 mod abs
} bind def

% proc-or-not -> bool   (an executable array: what drykit calls a procedure)
% @internal
/dkisproc {
    dup xcheck exch type dup /arraytype eq exch /packedarraytype eq or and
} bind def

% dict key default lo hi /error -> number   (a number option in lo..hi)
% The error is raised by executing its name, so it reads as itself.
% @internal
/dkoptnum {
    /dkoe exch def /dkoh exch def /dkol exch def
    dkget
    dup dkisnum not { pop dkoe cvx exec } if
    dup dkol lt 1 index dkoh gt or { pop dkoe cvx exec } if
} bind def

% value /error -> value   (an rgb array of three numbers 0..1)
% @internal
/dkrgb {
    /dkoe exch def
    dup type /arraytype ne { dkoe cvx exec } if
    dup xcheck { dkoe cvx exec } if
    dup length 3 ne { dkoe cvx exec } if
    dup {
        dup dkisnum not { pop dkoe cvx exec } if
        dup 0 lt exch 1 gt or { dkoe cvx exec } if
    } forall
    aload pop 3 array astore
} bind def

% a b t -> [a + (b - a) t]   (rgb arrays)
% @internal
/dklerp3 {
    /dklt exch def /dklb exch def /dkla exch def
    [ 0 1 2 { /dklk exch def
        dkla dklk get dklb dklk get dkla dklk get sub dklt mul add } for ]
} bind def

% -   (resolves one subpath, stops dkSall[dkSa .. dkSb], into runs on the
% operand stack, each `[key run]`; called inside the record's `[ ... ]`)
% @internal
/dkSsub {
    /dkSm dkSb dkSa sub 1 add def
    % seed
    dkSo /Seed known {
        /dkSseed dkSo /Seed get cvi dkSk add def
    } {
        dkSall dkSa get aload pop pop pop pop pop
        transform userdict /pjCTM get itransform
        dkSquant exch dkSquant 46337 mul add
        /dkSseed exch def
    } ifelse
    % per stop: touch key, width, effective width
    /dkStk dkSm array def
    /dkSwe dkSm array def
    0 1 dkSm 1 sub {
        /dkSi exch def
        /dkSst dkSall dkSa dkSi add get def
        /dkSt dkSst 3 get def
        dkStp {
            dkSt dkStouch
            dup dkisnum not { pop dkstroke-touch-procedure-must-return-a-number } if
            dup 0 lt { pop 0 } if dup 1 gt { pop 1 } if
            dkSbands mul floor cvi dup dkSbands 1 sub gt { pop dkSbands 1 sub } if
            0.5 add dkSbands div
        } { dkStouch } ifelse
        dkStk dkSi 3 -1 roll put
        dkSpp {
            dkSt dkSpress
            dup dkisnum not { pop dkstroke-pressure-procedure-must-return-a-number } if
            dup 0 lt { pop 0 } if
        } { 1 } ifelse
        dkSw mul dkSwear dkSt mul 1 add mul
        1 dkStilt sub mul dkSside dkStilt mul add
        dkSwe dkSi 3 -1 roll put
    } for
    % fallout keeps the subpath's centerline and effective widths
    dkSfallout 0 gt {
        dkSfall dkSfn [ 0 1 dkSm 1 sub {
            /dkSi exch def
            dkSall dkSa dkSi add get dup 0 get exch 1 get dkSwe dkSi get 3 array astore
        } for ] dkSseed 2 array astore put
        /dkSfn dkSfn 1 add def
    } if
    % lanes
    0 1 dkSlanes 1 sub {
        /dkSl exch def
        /dkSlo dkSl 0.5 add dkSlanes div 0.5 sub def
        /dkSdt dkSlanes 3 ge dkStilt 0 gt and {
            dkSl 0 eq dkSl dkSlanes 1 sub eq or { 0.06 } { -0.06 } ifelse dkStilt mul
        } { 0 } ifelse def
        dkSl 1 add dksubseed
        /dkSon dkrand dkSload lt def
        /dkSopen false def
        /dkSkey 0 def
        0 1 dkSm 1 sub {
            /dkSi exch def
            /dkSst dkSall dkSa dkSi add get def
            dkSi 0 gt {
                dkrand
                dkSon
                    { dkSdropout dkSst 4 get mul dkSw div lt { /dkSon false def } if }
                    { dkSload dkSst 4 get mul dkSw div lt { /dkSon true def } if }
                ifelse
            } if
            dkSon {
                % this lane's stop: offset across the patch, its own half-width
                /dkSa0 dkSst 2 get def
                /dkSwi dkSwe dkSi get def
                dkSst 0 get dkSa0 sin neg dkSlo dkSwi mul mul add
                dkSst 1 get dkSa0 cos dkSlo dkSwi mul mul add
                dkSwi dkSlanes div 2 div dkSlanes 1 gt { 1.18 mul } if
                3 array astore
                /dkSnew exch def
                /dkSk2 dkStk dkSi get dkSdt add dup 0 lt { pop 0 } if def
                dkSopen {
                    dkSnew
                    dkSk2 dkSkey ne {
                        % the band changes here: the segment into this stop
                        % was the old band's; close it and start the new one
                        dktomark dkSkey exch 2 array astore
                        mark dkSnew
                        /dkSkey dkSk2 def
                    } if
                } {
                    mark dkSnew
                    /dkSopen true def
                    /dkSkey dkSk2 def
                } ifelse
            } {
                dkSopen { dktomark dkSkey exch 2 array astore /dkSopen false def } if
            } ifelse
        } for
        dkSopen { dktomark dkSkey exch 2 array astore } if
    } for
} bind def

% opts -   (validates every key, then walks and resolves the current path
% into a record; renders it, or adds it to the open dkbatch)
% @internal
/dkSrecord {
    /dkSo exch def
    /dkSo load type /dicttype ne { dkstroke-options-must-be-a-dict } if
    userdict /pjCTM known not { dkstroke-needs-a-surface } if
    /dkSw dkSo /Width 2 1e-6 1e6 /dkstroke-width-must-be-positive dkoptnum def
    /dkStouch dkSo /Touch 0.8 dkget def
    /dkStouch load dkisproc {
        /dkStp true def
    } {
        /dkStp false def
        /dkStouch load dkisnum not { dkstroke-touch-must-be-a-number-or-procedure } if
        dkStouch 0 lt dkStouch 1 gt or { dkstroke-touch-must-be-0-to-1 } if
    } ifelse
    /dkSbands dkSo /Bands 4 1 16 /dkstroke-bands-must-be-1-to-16 dkoptnum def
    dkSbands dup cvi ne { dkstroke-bands-must-be-1-to-16 } if
    /dkSbands dkSbands cvi def
    dkSo /Pressure known {
        /dkSpress dkSo /Pressure get def
        /dkSpress load dkisproc not { dkstroke-pressure-must-be-a-procedure } if
        /dkSpp true def
    } { /dkSpp false def } ifelse
    /dkSwear dkSo /Wear 0 0 4 /dkstroke-wear-must-be-0-to-4 dkoptnum def
    /dkStilt dkSo /Tilt 0 0 90 /dkstroke-tilt-must-be-0-to-90 dkoptnum def
    /dkSside dkSo /Side 8 1e-6 1e6 /dkstroke-side-must-be-positive dkoptnum def
    /dkSstreak dkSo /Streak 1.4 1 4 /dkstroke-streak-must-be-1-to-4 dkoptnum def
    /dkSlevels dkSo /Levels 2 1 4 /dkstroke-levels-must-be-1-to-4 dkoptnum def
    dkSlevels dup cvi ne { dkstroke-levels-must-be-1-to-4 } if
    /dkSlevels dkSlevels cvi def
    /dkSstrength dkSo /Strength 0.85 0 1 /dkstroke-strength-must-be-0-to-1 dkoptnum def
    dkSo /Under known {
        dkSo /Under get /dkstroke-under-must-be-an-rgb-array dkrgb
    } {
        userdict /dkGround known not { dkstroke-needs-a-surface } if
        userdict /dkGround get
    } ifelse
    /dkSunder exch def
    /dkShalo dkSo /Halo 0.25 0 4 /dkstroke-halo-must-be-0-to-4 dkoptnum def
    /dkSload dkSo /Load 1 0 1 /dkstroke-load-must-be-0-to-1 dkoptnum def
    /dkSdropout dkSo /Dropout 0 0 1 /dkstroke-dropout-must-be-0-to-1 dkoptnum def
    /dkSlanes dkSo /Lanes 1 1 12 /dkstroke-lanes-must-be-1-to-12 dkoptnum def
    dkSlanes dup cvi ne { dkstroke-lanes-must-be-1-to-12 } if
    /dkSlanes dkSlanes cvi def
    /dkSfallout dkSo /Fallout 0 0 20 /dkstroke-fallout-must-be-0-to-20 dkoptnum def
    /dkSdrift dkSo /Drift 0 0 1e6 /dkstroke-drift-must-not-be-negative dkoptnum def
    /dkSafter dkSo /After false dkget def
    /dkSafter load type /booleantype ne { dkstroke-after-must-be-a-boolean } if
    dkSo /Seed known {
        dkSo /Seed get dup dkisnum not { pop dkstroke-seed-must-be-a-number } if
        abs 2147483647 ge { dkstroke-seed-must-be-within-integer-range } if
    } if
    % Tilt: s = sin(Tilt) blends the tip's width toward /Side; a tilted
    % stick presses at the edges of its patch, so it gets at least three
    % lanes (edge, face, edge) to carry that.
    /dkStilt dkStilt sin def
    dkStilt 0 gt dkSlanes 3 lt and { /dkSlanes 3 def } if

    % Walk: count, then fill a preallocated array (artkit's walkpath warns
    % that a proc which leaves anything on the stack breaks multi-subpath
    % paths, so the stops are not collected with `[ ... ]` around it).
    % The pitch sets how finely touch, pressure and the contact chain vary
    % along the stroke, not the ink's smoothness (the ink is the walked
    % centerline, which follows the flattened path's own corners closely
    % enough at this spacing). 1pt is fine for glyph-sized strokes; a finer
    % one costs walk and catch time for no visible change.
    /dkSpitch dkSw 0.75 mul dup 1 lt { pop 1 } if dup 4 gt { pop 4 } if def
    /dkSn 0 def
    dkSpitch { pop pop pop pop pop pop /dkSn dkSn 1 add def } walkpath
    /dkSall dkSn array def
    /dkSi 0 def
    dkSpitch {
        6 array astore dkSall dkSi 3 -1 roll put /dkSi dkSi 1 add def
    } walkpath
    newpath

    /dkSrec 16 dict def
    dkSrec /ctm matrix currentmatrix put
    dkSrec /pig [ currentrgbcolor ] put
    dkSrec /under dkSunder put
    dkSrec /strength dkSstrength put
    dkSrec /levels dkSlevels put
    dkSrec /halo dkShalo dkSw mul 2 div put
    dkSrec /streak dkSstreak put
    dkSrec /width dkSw put
    dkSrec /fallout dkSfallout put
    dkSrec /drift dkSdrift put
    1 0 dtransform userdict /pjCTM get idtransform
    0 1 dtransform userdict /pjCTM get idtransform dksvmax
    dkSrec /sv 3 -1 roll put
    /dkSfall dkSn 1 dkmax array def
    /dkSfn 0 def
    % subpaths start at a stop flagged 1 (first) or 3 (a single point)
    /dkSstarts [
        0 1 dkSn 1 sub {
            dup dkSall exch get 5 get dup 1 eq exch 3 eq or { } { pop } ifelse
        } for
    ] def
    dkSrec /runs [
        0 1 dkSstarts length 1 sub {
            /dkSk exch def
            /dkSa dkSstarts dkSk get def
            /dkSb dkSk 1 add dkSstarts length lt
                { dkSstarts dkSk 1 add get 1 sub } { dkSn 1 sub } ifelse def
            dkSsub
        } for
    ] put
    dkSrec /falls dkSfall 0 dkSfn getinterval put

    userdict /dkBatch known {
        userdict /dkBatch get /dkBb exch def
        % The dkclip region in force (#312), unless it is the one the batch
        % itself was opened in: that one is still in force when the batch
        % renders, and clipping to it twice would thin its edges.
        % A plain clip changed inside the batch (#444): the gstate taken at
        % the first stroke after the change, shared until the next one.
        % In pscat a capture whose clip is no longer in force (a grestore
        % drykit has no shadow for, #488) is taken again.
        dkSrec /clip
            dkBb /pc get null eq {
                userdict /dkClip known { userdict /dkClip get } { null } ifelse
                dup dkBb /base get eq { pop null } if
            } {
                dkBb /pc get dup type /gstatetype eq
                    { dkPsame not { dkBb /pc /dirty put } if } { pop } ifelse
                dkBb /pc get /dirty eq { dkBb /pc gstate put } if
                dkBb /pc get
            } ifelse
        put
        dkSafter {
            % /After (#393): drawn at once after the batch renders, in call
            % order, so it neither checks nor sets the batch's pigment.
            dkBb /after known not { dkBb /after 8 dict put } if
            dkBb /after get dup length dkSrec put
        } {
            dkBb /pig known {
                dkBb /pig get dkSrec /pig get
                true 0 1 2 { 3 index 1 index get 3 index 3 -1 roll get eq and } for
                3 1 roll pop pop
                not { dkbatch-mixes-pigments } if
            } { dkBb /pig dkSrec /pig get put } ifelse
            dkBb dkBb /n get dkSrec put
            dkBb /n dkBb /n get 1 add put
        } ifelse
    } {
        dkSrec /clip null put
        [ dkSrec ] dkrender
    } ifelse
} bind def

% e1 e2 -> bool   (same touch, streak and colour: may share one catch)
% @internal
/dkZsame {
    /dkZe2 exch def /dkZe1 exch def
    true 0 1 4 { dup dkZe1 exch get exch dkZe2 exch get eq and } for
    % and the same dkclip region (#312), compared only when the rest match
    dup { pop dkZe1 5 get /clip get dkZe2 5 get /clip get eq } if
} bind def

% entry -   (intersects the clip with a record's dkclip region, #312)
% Each link from the entry up to the batch's own base (dkZbase, set by
% dkbatch) is replayed in device space, where dkclip captured it, and
% clipped to. Leaves the CTM at identity and the path empty: the caller
% sets its own space next.
% @internal
/dkZclipin {
    mark exch
    {
        dup null eq { pop exit } if
        dup dkZbase eq { pop exit } if
        dup 1 get exch 0 get
    } loop
    matrix setmatrix
    { counttomark 0 eq { exit } if newpath exec clip } loop
    pop newpath
} bind def

% clip -   (a record's /clip at render time: a gstate, #444, or a dkclip entry)
% A gstate is put back whole, so the clip is exactly the one in force when
% the stroke was made (it replaces the clip in force, never intersects
% it); the CTM, colour and path it also brings back are the caller's to
% set next, as after dkZclipin.
% @internal
/dkZclipat {
    dup type /gstatetype eq { setgstate newpath } { dkZclipin } ifelse
} bind def

% A plain clip inside a dkbatch (#444). While a batch's procedure runs,
% dkbatch puts these into userdict in place of the clip operators and
% gsave/grestore (only if every one of those names still resolves to
% systemdict). The batch dict tracks /pc, the plain clip in force:
%   null    no plain clip change (the #312 rule: the dkclip entry, if any)
%   /dirty  changed since the last capture: the next dkstroke takes a gstate
%   gstate  that capture, shared by every stroke until the clip changes
% so strokes under one clip share one gstate object, and dkZsame's
% identity test still groups them. /pcs is a stack of /pc values, pushed
% by gsave and popped by grestore ([rest pc] links). A change the shadows
% cannot follow goes to /dirty, never to null: /dirty only costs grouping.
% Procedures bound before the batch reach the operators directly and are
% not seen (the old behaviour: the clip in force when the batch ends). An
% unseen grestore after a seen clip would leave /pc on a stale capture:
% standard PostScript cannot detect it (#459,
% notes/459-bound-wrapper-grestore.md), but pscat's .sameclip can, so
% there dkstroke takes the capture again when its clip is no longer in
% force (#488, notes/488-sameclip.md). Under Ghostscript the capture stays
% stale until the next change drykit sees.
% @internal
systemdict /.sameclip known /dkPsameok exch def
% gstate -> bool   (the clip in force is the gstate's; true without .sameclip)
% @internal
/dkPsame { dkPsameok { .sameclip } { pop true } ifelse } bind def
% @internal
/dkPdirty {
    userdict /dkBatch known { userdict /dkBatch get /pc /dirty put } if
} bind def
% @internal
/dkPpush {
    userdict /dkBatch known {
        userdict /dkBatch get dup /pcs get 1 index /pc get 2 array astore
        /pcs exch put
    } if
} bind def
% @internal
/dkPpop {
    userdict /dkBatch known {
        userdict /dkBatch get dup /pcs get dup null eq
            { pop /pc /dirty put }
            { 2 copy 0 get /pcs exch put 1 get /pc exch put } ifelse
    } if
} bind def
% @internal
/dkPclip { clip dkPdirty } bind def
% @internal
/dkPeoclip { eoclip dkPdirty } bind def
% @internal
/dkPrectclip { rectclip dkPdirty } bind def
% @internal
/dkPinitclip { initclip dkPdirty } bind def
% @internal
/dkPsetgstate { setgstate dkPdirty } bind def
% @internal
/dkPinitgraphics { initgraphics dkPdirty } bind def
% @internal
/dkPgsave { dkPpush gsave } bind def
% @internal
/dkPgrestore { grestore dkPpop } bind def
% @internal
/dkPgrestoreall {
    grestoreall
    userdict /dkBatch known { userdict /dkBatch get dup /pcs null put /pc /dirty put } if
} bind def
% [name shadow ...]   (the names dkbatch shadows, with their shadows)
% @internal
/dkPnames [
    /clip /dkPclip load /eoclip /dkPeoclip load /rectclip /dkPrectclip load
    /initclip /dkPinitclip load /setgstate /dkPsetgstate load
    /initgraphics /dkPinitgraphics load /gsave /dkPgsave load
    /grestore /dkPgrestore load /grestoreall /dkPgrestoreall load
] def
% -   (puts the shadows into userdict, if every name resolves to systemdict)
% @internal
/dkPon {
    true 0 2 dkPnames length 1 sub {
        dkPnames exch get where { systemdict eq } { false } ifelse and
    } for
    { 0 2 dkPnames length 1 sub {
        userdict exch dkPnames exch 2 getinterval aload pop put
    } for } if
} bind def
% -   (takes back every shadow dkPon put into userdict)
% @internal
/dkPoff {
    0 2 dkPnames length 1 sub {
        dkPnames exch 2 getinterval aload pop
        1 index userdict exch known {
            userdict 2 index get eq { userdict exch undef } { pop } ifelse
        } { pop pop } ifelse
    } for
} bind def

% run R -> estimated cells   (what a catch over the run visits)
% The run and R are in the run's own user space; dkZsvE is its stretch to
% canvas space, so the cell size is converted rather than every stop.
% Length x 2R plus the round ends, over the cell area: the cells within R
% of the centerline. Overlap between runs only lowers the real count.
% @internal
/dkZest {
    /dkZR exch def /dkZer exch def
    0
    0 1 dkZer length 2 sub {
        /dkZq exch def
        dkZer dkZq 1 add get 0 get dkZer dkZq get 0 get sub dup mul
        dkZer dkZq 1 add get 1 get dkZer dkZq get 1 get sub dup mul add sqrt
        add
    } for
    dkZR 2 mul mul dkZR dup mul 3.1416 mul add
    userdict /pjW get dkZsvE div dup mul div
} bind def

% entries -   (one catch over the entries' runs, then their ink through it)
% Entry: [touch streak r g b rec run hwadd].
% @internal
/dkZdraw {
    /dkZg exch def
    gsave
        dkZg 0 get 5 get /clip get dup null eq { pop } { dkZclipat } ifelse
        dkZg 0 get dup 2 get exch dup 3 get exch 4 get setrgbcolor
        userdict /pjCTM get setmatrix
        /dkZKc dkZg 0 get 1 get 1.1 mul 0.22 add userdict /pjW get mul def
        [
            dkZg {
                /dkZde exch def
                /dkZm dkZde 5 get /ctm get def
                /dkZsv dkZde 5 get /sv get def
                /dkZha dkZde 7 get def
                [ dkZde 6 get {
                    aload pop dkZha add dkZsv mul
                    3 1 roll dkZm transform userdict /pjCTM get itransform 3 -1 roll
                    3 array astore
                } forall ] dkZthin
            } forall
        ]
        % A run too wide for any chunk still reaches dkcatch, whose budget
        % guard names the problem; the gsave is given back before it
        % propagates (levels already drawn stay drawn).
        dkZg 0 get 0 get dkZg 0 get 1 get
        { dkcatch } stopped { grestore stop } if
        dkZg {
            /dkZde exch def
            dkZde 5 get /ctm get setmatrix
            /dkZha dkZde 7 get def
            dkZde 6 get dkZink
        } forall
    grestore
} bind def

% canvas-run -> canvas-run   (fewer stops for the catch, same reach)
% walkpath's pitch is set for the ink, and is far finer than the catch
% needs: a capsule per short segment revisits the same cells many times
% (measured 19 us per cell, against 3.5 for long segments). So the catch
% keeps about one stop per twice its reach, and each kept stop's
% half-width grows by the widest stop and the farthest chord deviation in
% the windows on either side of it, so the thinned centerline still
% reaches every cell the full one did.
% @internal
/dkZthin {
    /dkZtr exch def
    /dkZtn dkZtr length def
    dkZtn 3 lt {
        dkZtr
    } {
        /dkZtl 0 def /dkZth 0 def
        0 1 dkZtn 2 sub {
            /dkZq exch def
            /dkZtl dkZtl
                dkZtr dkZq 1 add get 0 get dkZtr dkZq get 0 get sub dup mul
                dkZtr dkZq 1 add get 1 get dkZtr dkZq get 1 get sub dup mul add sqrt
                add def
        } for
        dkZtr { 2 get dup dkZth gt { /dkZth exch def } { pop } ifelse } forall
        /dkZtk dkZth dkZKc add 2 mul dkZtl dkZtn 1 sub div 1e-9 dkmax div floor cvi 1 dkmax def
        dkZtk 1 eq {
            dkZtr
        } {
            % kept indices: 0, k, 2k, ..., and the last
            /dkZti [ 0 dkZtk dkZtn 2 sub { } for dkZtn 1 sub ] def
            /dkZtw dkZti length 1 sub array def
            0 1 dkZti length 2 sub {
                /dkZq exch def
                /dkZa0 dkZti dkZq get def /dkZa1 dkZti dkZq 1 add get def
                /dkZax dkZtr dkZa0 get 0 get def /dkZay dkZtr dkZa0 get 1 get def
                /dkZbx dkZtr dkZa1 get 0 get dkZax sub def
                /dkZby dkZtr dkZa1 get 1 get dkZay sub def
                /dkZbl dkZbx dup mul dkZby dup mul add def
                /dkZwm 0 def
                dkZa0 1 dkZa1 {
                    dkZtr exch get aload pop
                    /dkZch exch def /dkZcy exch dkZay sub def /dkZcx exch dkZax sub def
                    dkZbl 0 gt {
                        dkZcx dkZbx mul dkZcy dkZby mul add dkZbl div
                        dup 0 lt { pop 0 } if dup 1 gt { pop 1 } if
                        dup dkZbx mul dkZcx exch sub dup mul
                        exch dkZby mul dkZcy exch sub dup mul add sqrt
                    } {
                        dkZcx dup mul dkZcy dup mul add sqrt
                    } ifelse
                    dkZch add dup dkZwm gt { /dkZwm exch def } { pop } ifelse
                } for
                dkZtw dkZq dkZwm put
            } for
            [
                0 1 dkZti length 1 sub {
                    /dkZq exch def
                    dkZtr dkZti dkZq get get dup 0 get exch 1 get
                    dkZq 0 gt { dkZtw dkZq 1 sub get } { 0 } ifelse
                    dkZq dkZti length 1 sub lt { dkZtw dkZq get } { 0 } ifelse
                    dkmax
                    3 array astore
                } for
            ]
        } ifelse
    } ifelse
} bind def

% run -   (paints one run's ink, in the current (the run's own) space)
% A run of one stop is a dot. Otherwise a constant-width run is a
% round-capped stroke, and a varying one is the union of a disc at every
% stop and a quadrilateral along every segment, all counter-clockwise so
% the nonzero fill is their union: the ink stays within each segment's
% wider end, the reach dkcatch was cut for.
% @internal
/dkZink {
    /dkZir exch def
    /dkZconst true def
    dkZir { 2 get dkZir 0 get 2 get ne { /dkZconst false def } if } forall
    dkZir length 1 eq dkZconst not or {
        newpath
        dkZir {
            aload pop dkZha add /dkZih exch def /dkZiy exch def /dkZix exch def
            dkZih 0 gt {
                dkZix dkZih add dkZiy moveto
                dkZix dkZiy dkZih 0 360 arc closepath
            } if
        } forall
        0 1 dkZir length 2 sub {
            /dkZq exch def
            dkZir dkZq get aload pop dkZha add /dkZh0 exch def /dkZy0 exch def /dkZx0 exch def
            dkZir dkZq 1 add get aload pop dkZha add /dkZh1 exch def /dkZy1 exch def /dkZx1 exch def
            /dkZdx dkZx1 dkZx0 sub def /dkZdy dkZy1 dkZy0 sub def
            /dkZl dkZdx dup mul dkZdy dup mul add sqrt def
            dkZl 0 gt {
                /dkZnx dkZdy neg dkZl div def /dkZny dkZdx dkZl div def
                dkZx0 dkZnx dkZh0 mul sub dkZy0 dkZny dkZh0 mul sub moveto
                dkZx1 dkZnx dkZh1 mul sub dkZy1 dkZny dkZh1 mul sub lineto
                dkZx1 dkZnx dkZh1 mul add dkZy1 dkZny dkZh1 mul add lineto
                dkZx0 dkZnx dkZh0 mul add dkZy0 dkZny dkZh0 mul add lineto
                closepath
            } if
        } for
        fill
    } {
        dkZir 0 get 2 get dkZha add dup 0 gt {
            2 mul setlinewidth 1 setlinecap 1 setlinejoin
            newpath
            dkZir 0 get 0 get dkZir 0 get 1 get moveto
            dkZir { aload pop pop lineto } forall
            stroke
        } { pop } ifelse
    } ifelse
} bind def

% entries -   (dkZdraw in chunks whose estimated cells fit dkbudget)
% @internal
/dkZgroup {
    /dkZgs exch def
    /dkZK dkZgs 0 get 1 get 1.1 mul 0.22 add userdict /pjW get mul def
    /dkZsum 0 def
    /dkZcut dkbudget 0.6 mul def
    mark
    dkZgs {
        /dkZe exch def
        /dkZrr dkZe 6 get def
        /dkZhr dkZe 7 get def
        /dkZmaxh 0 def
        dkZrr { 2 get dkZhr add dup dkZmaxh gt { /dkZmaxh exch def } { pop } ifelse } forall
        /dkZsvE dkZe 5 get /sv get def
        /dkZRr dkZmaxh dkZK dkZsvE div add def
        dkZrr dkZRr dkZest
        dup dkZcut gt dkZrr length 2 gt and {
            % one long run: split it into pieces that share an end stop
            pop
            /dkZpe dkZrr length 1 sub def
            /dkZp0 0 def
            {
                dkZp0 dkZpe ge { exit } if
                /dkZp1 dkZp0 1 add def
                {
                    dkZp1 dkZpe ge { exit } if
                    dkZrr dkZp0 dkZp1 dkZp0 sub 2 add getinterval dkZRr dkZest
                    dkZcut gt { exit } if
                    /dkZp1 dkZp1 1 add def
                } loop
                /dkZpiece dkZrr dkZp0 dkZp1 dkZp0 sub 1 add getinterval def
                /dkZpc dkZpiece dkZRr dkZest def
                counttomark 0 gt dkZsum dkZpc add dkZcut gt and {
                    dktomark dkZdraw mark /dkZsum 0 def
                } if
                [ dkZe aload pop pop pop dkZpiece dkZhr ]
                /dkZsum dkZsum dkZpc add def
                /dkZp0 dkZp1 def
            } loop
        } {
            /dkZc exch def
            counttomark 0 gt dkZsum dkZc add dkZcut gt and {
                dktomark dkZdraw mark /dkZsum 0 def
            } if
            dkZe
            /dkZsum dkZsum dkZc add def
        } ifelse
    } forall
    counttomark 0 gt { dktomark dkZdraw } { pop } ifelse
} bind def

% records -   (draws records level-major, then their fallout)
% @internal
/dkrender {
    /dkZrecs exch def
    /dkZmax 0 def
    dkZrecs { /levels get dup dkZmax gt { /dkZmax exch def } { pop } ifelse } forall
    1 1 dkZmax {
        /dkZp exch def
        /dkZents [
            dkZrecs {
                /dkZr exch def
                /dkZL dkZr /levels get def
                /dkZj dkZp dkZmax dkZL sub sub def
                dkZj 1 ge {
                    /dkZoff dkZL dkZj sub 0.12 mul def
                    /dkZcol dkZr /under get dkZr /pig get
                        dkZr /strength get dkZj mul dkZL div dklerp3 def
                    /dkZha dkZj 1 eq dkZL 2 ge and { dkZr /halo get } { 0 } ifelse def
                    dkZr /runs get {
                        aload pop /dkZrun exch def
                        dkZoff add dkZr /streak get dkZcol aload pop
                        dkZr dkZrun dkZha 8 array astore
                    } forall
                } if
            } forall
        ] def
        /dkZdone dkZents length array def
        0 1 dkZents length 1 sub {
            /dkZa exch def
            dkZdone dkZa get true ne {
                /dkZe0 dkZents dkZa get def
                [
                    dkZa 1 dkZents length 1 sub {
                        /dkZb exch def
                        dkZdone dkZb get true ne {
                            dkZents dkZb get dup dkZe0 dkZsame
                                { dkZdone dkZb true put } { pop } ifelse
                        } if
                    } for
                ] dkZgroup
            } if
        } for
    } for
    dkZrecs { dkZfallout } forall
} bind def

% rec -   (the record's loose particles, through artkit's scatter)
% Each ~20pt piece of each subpath's centerline gets round(Fallout x its
% length) particles in a rectangle along it, thinning away from the line
% (/Weight), each nudged down canvas-space y by up to /Drift (/Scale
% carries the nudge's fraction). /Seed comes from the subpath's seed and
% the piece's index, and scatter restores the caller's stream.
% @internal
/dkZfallout {
    /dkZr exch def
    dkZr /fallout get 0 gt {
        dkZr /clip get dup null eq { pop } { gsave dkZclipat } ifelse
        /dkZfcol dkZr /under get dkZr /pig get dkZr /strength get 0.7 mul dklerp3 def
        /dkZfr dkZr /width get 0.05 mul dup 0.12 lt { pop 0.12 } if def
        dkZr /falls get {
            aload pop /dkSseed exch def /dkZfs exch def
            /dkZfi 0 def
            /dkZp0 0 def
            /dkZfn dkZfs length def
            dkZfn 1 gt {
                {
                    dkZp0 dkZfn 1 sub ge { exit } if
                    /dkZp1 dkZp0 def /dkZflen 0 def /dkZfh 0 def
                    {
                        dkZp1 dkZfn 1 sub ge dkZflen 20 ge or { exit } if
                        /dkZflen dkZflen
                            dkZfs dkZp1 1 add get 0 get dkZfs dkZp1 get 0 get sub dup mul
                            dkZfs dkZp1 1 add get 1 get dkZfs dkZp1 get 1 get sub dup mul add sqrt
                            add def
                        dkZfs dkZp1 get 2 get dup dkZfh gt { /dkZfh exch def } { pop } ifelse
                        /dkZp1 dkZp1 1 add def
                    } loop
                    /dkZfh dkZfh 0.9 mul def
                    /dkZfc dkZflen dkZr /fallout get mul round cvi def
                    /dkZfi dkZfi 1 add def
                    dkZfc 0 gt dkZflen 0 gt and dkZfh 0 gt and {
                        gsave
                            dkZr /ctm get setmatrix
                            dkZfcol aload pop setrgbcolor
                            dkZfs dkZp0 get 0 get dkZfs dkZp0 get 1 get translate
                            dkZfs dkZp1 get 1 get dkZfs dkZp0 get 1 get sub
                            dkZfs dkZp1 get 0 get dkZfs dkZp0 get 0 get sub atan rotate
                            0 dkZr /drift get neg userdict /pjCTM get dtransform idtransform
                            /dkZdy exch def /dkZdx exch def
                            0 dkZfh neg dkZflen dkZfh 2 mul screct
                            <<
                                /Count dkZfc
                                /Seed 100000 dkZfi add dksubseed dkrand 2147483646 mul cvi
                                /Scale [0 1]
                                /Weight { exch pop abs dkZfh div 1 exch sub }
                                /Mark {
                                    pop /dkZms exch def
                                    dkZms dkZdy mul add exch dkZms dkZdx mul add exch
                                    /dkZmy exch def /dkZmx exch def
                                    newpath dkZmx dkZfr add dkZmy moveto
                                    dkZmx dkZmy dkZfr 0 360 arc fill
                                }
                            >> scatter
                        grestore
                    } if
                    /dkZp0 dkZp1 def
                } loop
            } if
        } forall
        dkZr /clip get null ne { grestore } if
    } if
} bind def

%%SelfTest: dkstroke-rejects-malformed-options
%   << /Surface /drawing >> dksurface
%   newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto
%   { 5 dkstroke } /dkstroke-options-must-be-a-dict (a number for the options) mustguard
%   { << /Width 0 >> dkstroke } /dkstroke-width-must-be-positive (/Width 0) mustguard
%   { << /Width { 2 } >> dkstroke } /dkstroke-width-must-be-positive (a procedure /Width) mustguard
%   { << /Touch 1.2 >> dkstroke } /dkstroke-touch-must-be-0-to-1 (/Touch 1.2) mustguard
%   { << /Touch -0.1 >> dkstroke } /dkstroke-touch-must-be-0-to-1 (/Touch -0.1) mustguard
%   { << /Touch (x) >> dkstroke } /dkstroke-touch-must-be-a-number-or-procedure (a string /Touch) mustguard
%   { << /Pressure 2 >> dkstroke } /dkstroke-pressure-must-be-a-procedure (a number /Pressure) mustguard
%   { << /Levels 0 >> dkstroke } /dkstroke-levels-must-be-1-to-4 (/Levels 0) mustguard
%   { << /Levels 5 >> dkstroke } /dkstroke-levels-must-be-1-to-4 (/Levels 5) mustguard
%   { << /Levels 1.5 >> dkstroke } /dkstroke-levels-must-be-1-to-4 (/Levels 1.5) mustguard
%   { << /Bands 0 >> dkstroke } /dkstroke-bands-must-be-1-to-16 (/Bands 0) mustguard
%   { << /Bands 17 >> dkstroke } /dkstroke-bands-must-be-1-to-16 (/Bands 17) mustguard
%   { << /Streak 0.5 >> dkstroke } /dkstroke-streak-must-be-1-to-4 (/Streak 0.5) mustguard
%   { << /Tilt 120 >> dkstroke } /dkstroke-tilt-must-be-0-to-90 (/Tilt 120) mustguard
%   { << /Side 0 >> dkstroke } /dkstroke-side-must-be-positive (/Side 0) mustguard
%   { << /Wear -1 >> dkstroke } /dkstroke-wear-must-be-0-to-4 (/Wear -1) mustguard
%   { << /Strength 2 >> dkstroke } /dkstroke-strength-must-be-0-to-1 (/Strength 2) mustguard
%   { << /Under [1 1] >> dkstroke } /dkstroke-under-must-be-an-rgb-array (a two-entry /Under) mustguard
%   { << /Halo -0.2 >> dkstroke } /dkstroke-halo-must-be-0-to-4 (/Halo -0.2) mustguard
%   { << /Load 2 >> dkstroke } /dkstroke-load-must-be-0-to-1 (/Load 2) mustguard
%   { << /Dropout -1 >> dkstroke } /dkstroke-dropout-must-be-0-to-1 (/Dropout -1) mustguard
%   { << /Lanes 0 >> dkstroke } /dkstroke-lanes-must-be-1-to-12 (/Lanes 0) mustguard
%   { << /Fallout -1 >> dkstroke } /dkstroke-fallout-must-be-0-to-20 (/Fallout -1) mustguard
%   { << /Drift -3 >> dkstroke } /dkstroke-drift-must-not-be-negative (/Drift -3) mustguard
%   { << /After 1 >> dkstroke } /dkstroke-after-must-be-a-boolean (a number /After) mustguard
%   { << /Seed (s) >> dkstroke } /dkstroke-seed-must-be-a-number (a string /Seed) mustguard
%   { << /Seed 1e12 >> dkstroke } /dkstroke-seed-must-be-within-integer-range (/Seed 1e12) mustguard
%   { << /Touch { pop (x) } >> dkstroke } /dkstroke-touch-procedure-must-return-a-number
%   (a /Touch procedure returning a string) mustguard
%   { gsave << >> dkstroke grestore } (the defaults) mustpass
%%EndSelfTest
%
%%SelfTest: dkstroke-needs-a-surface
%   newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto
%   { << >> dkstroke } /dkstroke-needs-a-surface (a stroke before any surface) mustguard
%   << >> pkcanvas
%   { << >> dkstroke } /dkstroke-needs-a-surface (a canvas but no ground and no /Under) mustguard
%   { gsave newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /Under [1 1 1] >> dkstroke grestore }
%   (a bare pkcanvas with an explicit /Under) mustpass
%%EndSelfTest
%
%%SelfTest: dkstroke-takes-no-draws-from-the-callers-stream
%   << /Surface /slate >> dksurface
%   1 srand rand /dkta exch def
%   1 srand
%   gsave newpath 10 10 moveto 90 40 lineto 30 80 moveto 80 80 lineto
%   << /Width 4 /Touch { 0.5 mul 0.4 add } /Pressure { 1 exch sub } /Dropout 0.3 /Load 0.7
%      /Lanes 3 /Tilt 40 /Fallout 0.5 /Drift 2 >> dkstroke grestore
%   rand dkta eq
%   (dkstroke, with every random feature on, leaves the caller's stream untouched) mustbe
%%EndSelfTest
%
%%SelfTest: dkstroke-a-run-past-the-budget-raises-cleanly
%   % A run too wide for any chunk reaches dkcatch's own budget guard, with
%   % dkZdraw's gsave given back (the block checks the graphics stack).
%   % Codex review of PR #286: the flush test once counted its own boolean
%   % as a queued entry and raised rangecheck on an empty queue instead.
%   << /Surface /drawing >> dksurface
%   /dkbudget 500 def
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 10 0 lineto << /Width 100 /Touch 0.5 >> dkstroke }
%   /dkcatch-area-exceeds-safety-limit (a run wider than any chunk) mustguard
%   { gsave newpath 0 0 moveto 10 0 lineto << /Width 2 /Touch 0.5 >> dkstroke grestore }
%   (a run inside the budget after a rejected one) mustpass
%%EndSelfTest
%
%%SelfTest: dkbatch-guards
%   << /Surface /slate >> dksurface
%   { 5 dkbatch } /dkbatch-needs-a-procedure (a number) mustguard
%   { { { } dkbatch } dkbatch } /dkbatch-cannot-nest (a batch inside a batch) mustguard
%   userdict /dkBatch known not
%   (a nested batch's error closes the outer batch) mustbe
%   { {
%       1 1 1 setrgbcolor newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << >> dkstroke
%       0 0 0 setrgbcolor newpath 0 9 moveto 50 9 lineto << >> dkstroke
%   } dkbatch } /dkbatch-mixes-pigments (two pigments in one batch) mustguard
%   userdict /dkBatch known not
%   (a failed batch leaves no batch open) mustbe
%   { gsave { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << >> dkstroke } dkbatch grestore }
%   (a one-stroke batch) mustpass
%   { gsave { } dkbatch grestore } (an empty batch) mustpass
%   % /After strokes (#393) neither check nor set the batch's pigment, in
%   % either order, and a batch of only /After strokes draws them
%   { gsave { 1 1 1 setrgbcolor newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /After true >> dkstroke
%       0 0 0 setrgbcolor newpath 0 9 moveto 50 9 lineto << >> dkstroke } dkbatch grestore }
%   (an /After stroke of another colour first) mustpass
%   { gsave { 0 0 0 setrgbcolor newpath 0 9 moveto 50 9 lineto << >> dkstroke
%       1 1 1 setrgbcolor newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /After true >> dkstroke } dkbatch grestore }
%   (an /After stroke of another colour last) mustpass
%   { gsave { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /After true >> dkstroke } dkbatch grestore }
%   (a batch of only /After strokes) mustpass
%   { gsave newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << /After true >> dkstroke grestore }
%   (/After with no batch open draws at once) mustpass
%   userdict /dkBatch known not (and no batch is left open) mustbe
%   % an /After stroke's render errors surface when the batch ends
%   /dkbudget 500 def
%   { { newpath 0 0 moveto 10 0 lineto << /Width 100 /Touch 0.5 /After true >> dkstroke } dkbatch }
%   /dkcatch-area-exceeds-safety-limit (an /After stroke past the budget) mustguard
%   userdict /dkBatch known not (and it leaves no batch open) mustbe
%%EndSelfTest
%
%%SelfTest: dkbatch-keeps-a-plain-clip
%   % #444: strokes under one plain clip share one gstate (so they can
%   % share a catch); a stroke after the grestore has none; a new clip
%   % takes a new gstate. dkBb is the batch dkbatch closed last.
%   << /Surface /slate >> dksurface
%   /dktbox { newpath 0 0 moveto 40 0 lineto 40 40 lineto closepath } def
%   /dktline { newpath 0 5 moveto 50 5 lineto << >> dkstroke } def
%   gsave
%   { gsave dktbox clip dktline dktline grestore dktline
%     gsave dktbox clip dktline grestore
%     /dktin /clip where { userdict eq } { false } ifelse def } dkbatch
%   grestore
%   dktin (inside a batch, clip is drykit's shadow) mustbe
%   dkBb 0 get /clip get type /gstatetype eq (a stroke under a plain clip keeps a gstate) mustbe
%   dkBb 0 get /clip get dkBb 1 get /clip get eq (two strokes under one clip share it) mustbe
%   dkBb 2 get /clip get null eq (a stroke after the grestore keeps none) mustbe
%   dkBb 3 get /clip get dkBb 0 get /clip get ne (a new clip takes a new gstate) mustbe
%   userdict /clip known userdict /gsave known or not
%   (the shadows are gone after the batch) mustbe
%   gsave
%   { { dktbox clip 1 0 div } dkbatch } /undefinedresult (an error in the batch) mustfail
%   grestore
%   userdict /clip known userdict /grestore known or not
%   (and after a batch that fails) mustbe
%   % a caller's own gsave in userdict: no shadows, the old rule
%   userdict /gsave systemdict /gsave get put
%   gsave { gsave dktbox clip dktline grestore } dkbatch grestore
%   userdict /gsave undef
%   dkBb 0 get /clip get null eq (with a userdict gsave the clip operators are left alone) mustbe
%%EndSelfTest
%
% @kind: Procedure
% @summary: Draws the current path as a dry stick (chalk, crayon, charcoal) dragged across the surface set by dksurface, in the current colour: pigment lands only where the stick's contact patch meets raised tooth, so light pressure breaks into streaks along the direction of travel and heavy pressure fills the valleys. Tone builds in deposit levels drawn faint-first, so crossings read darker, not lighter. Consumes the current path like fill; takes no rand draws from the caller's stream.
% @example: << /Surface /greenboard >> dksurface 0.93 0.94 0.9 setrgbcolor newpath 40 60 moveto 300 80 lineto << /Width 3 /Touch { 0.25 sub abs 0.9 exch sub } >> dkstroke
% @param: /Width [points] Contact width of the stick's tip; must be > 0 (default 2)
% @param: /Touch [0..1] Pressure against the tooth, the same quantity as paintkit's /Touch: low catches only the highest knuckles, 1 is solid. A procedure {t -> touch}, t = 0..1 along each subpath, gives a pressure profile, run once per stop and quantized to /Bands levels (default 0.8)
% @param: /Bands [count] Touch levels a /Touch procedure is quantized to, 1..16 (default 4)
% @param: /Pressure [proc] {t -> multiplier} width profile along each subpath, paintkit's meaning: a landing blob, a tapered lift. Run once per stop (default unset, constant width)
% @param: /Wear [fraction of /Width] How much wider the contact gets from the start of a subpath to its end as the tip flattens, 0..4 (default 0)
% @param: /Tilt [degrees] 0 draws with the tip; toward 90 the stick lies on its side, the contact widens toward /Side and the edges of the patch press harder than its face (default 0)
% @param: /Side [points] Length of the stick in contact when it lies on its side at /Tilt 90; must be > 0 (default 8)
% @param: /Streak [ratio] How much each tooth knuckle is stretched along the direction of travel, 1..4; 1 is round (default 1.4)
% @param: /Levels [count] Deposit levels, 1..4: the faintest reaches the most tooth and is drawn first, each brighter level lands on less (default 2)
% @param: /Strength [0..1] How strongly the top level reads against /Under: chalk is about 0.8, compressed charcoal about 0.95 (default 0.85)
% @param: /Under [rgb array] What lies beneath; lower levels lerp from it toward the pigment. drykit cannot read the page back, so it must be told (default the surface's /Ground)
% @param: /Halo [fraction of /Width] Extra width of the faintest level when /Levels is 2 or more: dust beside the stroke, 0..4 (default 0.25)
% @param: /Load [per /Width] 0..1 rate at which a lifted lane lands again per Width of travel, pkdry's meaning (default 1)
% @param: /Dropout [per /Width] 0..1 rate at which a lane lifts off per Width of travel, independent of the tooth (default 0)
% @param: /Lanes [count] Parallel lanes across the contact patch, 1..12, each with its own contact chain: crayon striation, split charcoal tails. A tilted stick uses at least 3 (default 1)
% @param: /Fallout [count per points] Loose particles per point of stroke length, 0..20, placed with artkit's scatter beside the stroke (default 0)
% @param: /Drift [points] How far fallout drifts down canvas-space y: chalk on a vertical board falls (default 0)
% @param: /Seed [integer] Seed for the tool-side randomness (contact chains, fallout); subpath i uses Seed + i. Leaves the caller's rand stream untouched (default from each subpath's first point on the canvas, so adding a stroke elsewhere never re-rolls this one)
% @param: /After [boolean] Inside a dkbatch, draw this stroke on its own after the batch's other strokes have rendered (after strokes in call order), as if it were made just after the batch closed: it keeps its colour, coordinate system and dkclip region, and may be a different colour from the batch, so an eraser or a smudge can be drawn from inside a batch over everything the batch lays. Ignored with no batch open (default false)
/dkstroke {
    dkSrecord
} bind def

% -   (renders the closed batch dkBb: its records level-major, then each
% /After record on its own, in call order)
% @internal
/dkBrender {
    [ 0 1 dkBb /n get 1 sub { dkBb exch get } for ] dkrender
    [ 0 1 dkBafter length 1 sub { dkBafter exch get } for ]
    { [ exch ] dkrender } forall
} bind def

% @kind: Procedure
% @summary: Runs a procedure whose dkstroke calls are drawn together, level-major: every stroke's faint level first, then every bright one, so crossing layers of hatching or re-stroked lines stay dark where they cross instead of the second layer's faint level greying the first's core. One pigment per batch: a stroke of another colour raises dkbatch-mixes-pigments unless it is an /After stroke, which is drawn on its own after the batch renders, in call order. Batches don't nest. Each stroke keeps the coordinate system it was given in, and the clip it was made under: the region of any dkclip, and a plain clip, eoclip or rectclip made inside the batch (strokes under one such clip still share their catches). A procedure bound before the batch reaches the clip operators and gsave/grestore directly, so drykit sees neither its clips nor its restores. In pscat a callback that clips and strokes inside a bound gsave ... exec ... grestore wrapper is still exact (pscat's .sameclip shows drykit the wrapper's grestore); under Ghostscript it leaves the batch's later strokes under that clip, since standard PostScript gives no way to see that grestore. For a program that must draw the same in both, use dkclip inside the callback, call the bound wrapper inside a gsave ... grestore of your own, or bind the wrapper inside the batch.
% @example: 0.12 0.12 0.13 setrgbcolor { 0 6 120 { newpath dup 0 moveto 120 add 120 lineto << /Width 1.2 >> dkstroke } for } dkbatch
/dkbatch {
    dup dkisproc not { pop dkbatch-needs-a-procedure } if
    userdict /dkBatch known { pop userdict /dkBatch undef dkbatch-cannot-nest } if
    % base: the dkclip region the batch opens in, still in force when it
    % renders, so its records need not re-clip to it (#312)
    % pc, pcs: the plain clip in force and its gsave stack, kept by the
    % shadows dkPon installs (#444); g: the graphics state the batch opens
    % in, for strokes made before a plain clip the batch ends under
    userdict /dkBatch 8 dict dup /n 0 put
        dup /base userdict /dkClip known { userdict /dkClip get } { null } ifelse put
        dup /pc null put dup /pcs null put dup /g gstate put
    put
    dkPon
    stopped { dkPoff userdict /dkBatch undef stop } if
    dkPoff
    userdict /dkBatch get /dkBb exch def
    userdict /dkBatch undef
    /dkZbase dkBb /base get def
    % /After strokes (#393), each drawn at once after the batch, in call
    % order, under the same base
    /dkBafter dkBb /after known { dkBb /after get } { 0 dict } ifelse def
    dkBb /pc get null eq {
        dkBrender
    } {
        % The batch ends under a plain clip it made (#444): render in the
        % state it opened in, so strokes made before that clip are not cut
        % by it (those made under it carry their own gstate).
        gsave dkBb /g get setgstate newpath
        { dkBrender } stopped grestore { stop } if
    } ifelse
} bind def

%%SelfTest: dkclip-guards
%   << /Surface /slate >> dksurface
%   { 5 dkclip } /dkclip-needs-a-procedure (a number) mustguard
%   { newpath { } dkclip } /dkclip-needs-a-path (no current path) mustguard
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto 50 50 lineto closepath { 1 0 div } dkclip }
%   /undefinedresult (an error inside the procedure) mustfail
%   userdict /dkClip known not
%   (a failed dkclip leaves no region in force) mustbe
%   { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto 50 50 lineto closepath
%     { { newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto << >> dkstroke
%         1 1 1 setrgbcolor newpath 0 9 moveto 50 9 lineto << >> dkstroke } dkbatch } dkclip }
%   /dkbatch-mixes-pigments (a batch inside a dkclip that fails) mustguard
%   userdict /dkClip known not userdict /dkBatch known not and
%   (and it leaves neither a region nor a batch open) mustbe
%   { gsave newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto 50 50 lineto closepath { } dkclip grestore }
%   (an empty procedure) mustpass
%%EndSelfTest
%
%%SelfTest: dkclip-scopes-its-region
%   << /Surface /slate >> dksurface
%   newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto 50 50 lineto closepath
%   { /dkta userdict /dkClip get def
%     newpath 10 10 moveto 20 10 lineto 20 20 lineto closepath
%     { /dktb userdict /dkClip get def } dkclip
%     /dktc userdict /dkClip get def } dkclip
%   dkta dktc eq (an inner dkclip gives the outer region back) mustbe
%   dktb 0 get dkta eq (the inner region links to the outer one) mustbe
%   userdict /dkClip known not (and none is left in force after) mustbe
%   newpath 0 0 moveto 50 0 lineto 50 50 lineto closepath
%   { /dktd { currentpoint } stopped { true } { pop pop false } ifelse def } dkclip
%   dktd (the procedure starts with no current path) mustbe
%   { currentpoint } stopped (and the path is consumed) mustbe
%%EndSelfTest
%
% @kind: Procedure
% @summary: Clips to the current path, as clip does, while a procedure runs, and keeps that region for every dkstroke the procedure makes inside an open dkbatch: the batch renders those strokes later, level-major with the rest, but each under its own region. So differently clipped strokes (overlapping hatched regions, a shape's interior and its background) can share one batch and keep their crossings dark. The region is the nonzero inside of the path, intersected with any dkclip already in force. Consumes the path; the procedure starts with none, and everything it changes in the graphics state is given back. Takes no rand draws.
% @example: << /Surface /drawing >> dksurface 0.1 0.1 0.1 setrgbcolor { newpath 20 20 moveto 120 20 lineto 120 120 lineto closepath { 0 4 140 { newpath dup 0 moveto 0 140 rlineto pop << /Width 1.5 >> dkstroke } for } dkclip newpath 60 20 moveto 160 20 lineto 160 120 lineto closepath { 0 4 140 { newpath 0 exch moveto 180 0 rlineto << /Width 1.5 >> dkstroke } for } dkclip } dkbatch
/dkclip {
    dup dkisproc not { pop dkclip-needs-a-procedure } if
    { pathbbox } stopped { pop dkclip-needs-a-path } { pop pop pop pop } ifelse
    % [parent path]: the path in device space, as operators (so a caller's
    % own moveto cannot change it), replayed by dkZclipin
    userdict /dkClip known { userdict /dkClip get } { null } ifelse
    gsave matrix setmatrix
    [
        { systemdict /moveto get }
        { systemdict /lineto get }
        { systemdict /curveto get }
        { systemdict /closepath get }
        pathforall
    ] cvx
    grestore
    2 array astore
    userdict /dkClip 3 -1 roll put
    % Inside a batch under a plain clip (#444), this region changes the
    % clip the next stroke must capture; the plain clip comes back after.
    dkPpush
    userdict /dkBatch known {
        userdict /dkBatch get /pc get null ne { dkPdirty } if
    } if
    gsave
    clip newpath
    stopped
    dkPpop
    userdict /dkClip get 0 get dup null eq
        { pop userdict /dkClip undef } { userdict exch /dkClip exch put } ifelse
    grestore
    newpath
    { stop } if
} bind def

%%SelfTest: dksurface-rejects-malformed-options
%   { 5 dksurface } /dksurface-options-must-be-a-dict
%   (a number for the options) mustguard
%
%   { << /Surface /marble >> dksurface } /dksurface-unknown-surface
%   (/Surface /marble) mustguard
%
%   { << /Surface (slate) >> dksurface } /dksurface-surface-must-be-a-name
%   (/Surface as a string) mustguard
%
%   { << /Ground [0.1 0.2] >> dksurface } /dksurface-ground-must-be-an-rgb-array
%   (a two-entry /Ground) mustguard
%
%   { << /Ground [0.1 0.2 1.5] >> dksurface } /dksurface-ground-must-be-an-rgb-array
%   (a /Ground channel above 1) mustguard
%
%   { << /Ground { 0.1 0.2 0.3 } >> dksurface } /dksurface-ground-must-be-an-rgb-array
%   (a procedure /Ground) mustguard
%
%   { << /Ground [0.1 (g) 0.3] >> dksurface } /dksurface-ground-must-be-an-rgb-array
%   (a string channel) mustguard
%
%   % pkcanvas's own guards still apply to the keys passed through.
%   { << /Weave 0 >> dksurface } /pkcanvas-weave-must-be-positive
%   (/Weave 0) mustguard
%
%   { << /Surface /slate /Weave 0.5 >> dksurface } (a surface with an override) mustpass
%   { << >> dksurface } (an empty dict) mustpass
%%EndSelfTest
%
%%SelfTest: dksurface-sets-the-surface-and-takes-no-draws
%   1 srand rand /dkta exch def
%   1 srand << /Surface /slate /Seed 4 >> dksurface rand dkta eq
%   (dksurface leaves the caller's stream untouched) mustbe
%
%   userdict /pjW get 0.4 eq userdict /pjR get 0.55 eq and userdict /pjM get 4 eq and
%   (/slate sets its weave, relief and mottle) mustbe
%   userdict /dkSurface get /slate eq
%   (and records its name) mustbe
%   userdict /dkGround get aload pop 0.16 eq exch 0.14 eq and exch 0.13 eq and
%   (and its ground) mustbe
%
%   << /Surface /drawing /Ground [0.5 0.6 0.7] /Weave 0.8 >> dksurface
%   userdict /pjW get 0.8 eq userdict /pjR get 0.65 eq and
%   (an override replaces one key and keeps the rest) mustbe
%   userdict /dkGround get 1 get 0.6 eq
%   (/Ground overrides the surface's colour) mustbe
%
%   % A rejected call leaves the previous surface whole.
%   { << /Surface /slate /Relief 2 >> dksurface } /pkcanvas-relief-must-be-0-to-1
%   (/Relief 2 on /slate) mustguard
%   userdict /dkSurface get /drawing eq userdict /pjW get 0.8 eq and
%   (a rejected dksurface keeps the old surface and ground) mustbe
%
%   << >> dksurface
%   userdict /dkSurface get /drawing eq userdict /pjW get 0.6 eq and
%   (the default surface is /drawing) mustbe
%%EndSelfTest
%
% @kind: Procedure
% @summary: Sets up the dry-media surface that drykit marks catch on: one of five named grounds (slate, green board, newsprint, drawing paper, construction paper), each a pkcanvas tooth plus the surface's own colour. Light pressure catches only the highest tooth, so a thin line breaks up, and two crossing strokes break up on the same tooth. Calls pkcanvas (so paintkit marks share the surface) and paints nothing; call it once, early, in the space the piece is drawn in. Takes no rand draws.
% @example: << /Surface /slate /Seed 3 >> dksurface
% @param: /Surface [name] Which ground: /slate, /greenboard, /newsprint, /drawing or /construction. It sets the defaults of every key below (default /drawing)
% @param: /Seed [integer] Seed for this surface alone, passed to pkcanvas; leaves the caller's rand stream untouched (default 1)
% @param: /Weave [points] Tooth spacing, one knuckle per Weave x Weave cell, passed to pkcanvas (default from /Surface: 0.4 for the boards, 0.35 newsprint, 0.6 drawing paper, 0.9 construction paper)
% @param: /Mottle [points] Scale of the slow variation in how proud the tooth stands, passed to pkcanvas (default from /Surface: 1.5 to 8)
% @param: /Relief [0..1] How much the slow mottle, rather than each knuckle's own height, decides which tooth stands proud, passed to pkcanvas (default from /Surface: 0.4 to 0.75)
% @param: /Ground [rgb array] The surface's own colour, three numbers 0..1. dksurface does not paint it; drykit marks read it as what lies beneath (default from /Surface: near-black slate, dark green-grey board, warm grey newsprint, off-white drawing paper, a blue construction paper)
/dksurface {
    /dkso exch def
    /dkso load type /dicttype ne { dksurface-options-must-be-a-dict } if
    /dksn dkso /Surface /drawing dkget def
    /dksn load type /nametype ne { dksurface-surface-must-be-a-name } if
    dksurfaces /dksn load known not { dksurface-unknown-surface } if
    /dksd dksurfaces /dksn load get def
    /dksg dkso /Ground dksd /Ground get dkget def
    /dksg load type /arraytype ne { dksurface-ground-must-be-an-rgb-array } if
    /dksg load xcheck { dksurface-ground-must-be-an-rgb-array } if
    /dksg load length 3 ne { dksurface-ground-must-be-an-rgb-array } if
    /dksg load {
        dup dkisnum not { pop dksurface-ground-must-be-an-rgb-array } if
        dup 0 lt exch 1 gt or { dksurface-ground-must-be-an-rgb-array } if
    } forall
    % pkcanvas runs every one of its guards before it writes anything, so
    % drykit's own state is written only after it succeeds.
    <<
        dkso /Seed known { /Seed dkso /Seed get } if
        /Weave dkso /Weave dksd /Weave get dkget
        /Mottle dkso /Mottle dksd /Mottle get dkget
        /Relief dkso /Relief dksd /Relief get dkget
    >> pkcanvas
    userdict /dkSurface /dksn load put
    userdict /dkGround [ /dksg load aload pop ] put
} bind def
